# Saved copies of official law sources are hash-verified, so they must stay
# byte-for-byte identical on every machine.
#
# foundry/tools/fetch-source.mjs writes <slug>.txt next to <slug>.json and records
# sha256(<slug>.txt) as meta.text_sha256. loadSnapshot() in foundry/tools/law-text.mjs
# re-hashes the file and refuses the snapshot if it differs, which is what makes a
# quoted statute checkable. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites those
# files to CRLF, the hash no longer matches, and cloudflare/scripts/check-law.mjs fails
# every claim in the state. Marking them -text stops git converting line endings in
# either direction; `diff` keeps them readable in diffs rather than treated as binary.
#
# Do not change this to `text eol=lf`: that normalises on commit, so a source that
# genuinely contains CRLF would be rewritten and its recorded hash broken for good.
foundry/out/law-audit/sources/** -text diff

# Server certificates fetched by foundry/tools/cert-chain.mjs: fingerprints are logged,
# so these must not be rewritten either.
foundry/out/law-audit/certs/** -text diff
